      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Transactions: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a Transaction Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "ACID",
                "Meaning"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "==A==tomic",
                  "all or nothing"
                ],
                [
                  "==C==onsistent",
                  "constraints hold before and after"
                ],
                [
                  "==I==solated",
                  "no peeking at half-done work"
                ],
                [
                  "==D==urable",
                  "committed data survives a crash"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A transaction = statements that ==succeed or fail as one unit==",
                "Changes stay {blue:private} until `COMMIT`",
                "`ROLLBACK` throws them all away"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Autocommit and Control",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:Autocommit}: each standalone statement is its own transaction",
                "`BEGIN` = manual control until `COMMIT` / `ROLLBACK`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "BEGIN;",
                "UPDATE accounts SET bal = bal - 100 WHERE id = 1;",
                "ROLLBACK;  -- the debit never happened"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. How the Database Does It",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Property",
                "Mechanism"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Atomicity",
                  "Undo info: old row versions (Postgres MVCC), undo log (MySQL InnoDB)"
                ],
                [
                  "Durability",
                  "Write-ahead log (==WAL==), flushed at COMMIT"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Change",
                    "sub": "in memory",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Log record",
                    "sub": "WAL",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "COMMIT",
                    "sub": "log flushed",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Data pages",
                    "sub": "written later",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Durability",
              "text": "Only the ==log== is flushed at COMMIT; data pages are written later."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "BEGIN, COMMIT, ROLLBACK and Savepoints",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "BEGIN, COMMIT, ROLLBACK and Savepoints",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Core workflow",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "BEGIN",
                    "sub": "or START TRANSACTION",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Statements",
                    "sub": "private until commit",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "COMMIT",
                    "sub": "persist",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "ROLLBACK",
                    "sub": "undo everything",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "BEGIN;",
                "UPDATE accounts SET bal = bal - 100 WHERE id = 1;",
                "UPDATE accounts SET bal = bal + 100 WHERE id = 2;",
                "COMMIT;"
              ],
              "note": "both updates persist together, or neither"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Savepoints",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`SAVEPOINT sp1` marks a point inside the transaction",
                "`ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT sp1` undoes ==only work after it==",
                "The transaction stays ==open== afterwards",
                "`RELEASE SAVEPOINT sp1` discards the marker"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Errors and DDL",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Postgres: an error aborts the whole transaction: `current transaction is aborted`",
                "Every later statement fails until ==ROLLBACK== or ==ROLLBACK TO== a savepoint",
                "Recovery from one failed statement: set a savepoint first, then `ROLLBACK TO` it"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Postgres",
                "MySQL"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "CREATE / ALTER / DROP",
                  "{green:Transactional}, can roll back",
                  "{red:Implicit commit}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "MySQL DDL",
              "text": "A DDL statement silently **commits** earlier work, so it can no longer be rolled back."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Isolation Levels and Read Anomalies",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Isolation Levels and Read Anomalies",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Three Read Anomalies",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Anomaly",
                "What you see",
                "Caused by"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "==Dirty read==",
                  "Another txn's uncommitted change, maybe rolled back",
                  "Uncommitted write"
                ],
                [
                  "==Non-repeatable read==",
                  "Same row, two reads, new value",
                  "Committed UPDATE/DELETE"
                ],
                [
                  "==Phantom read==",
                  "Same range query, different rows",
                  "Committed INSERT/DELETE"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Four Levels",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Level",
                "Dirty",
                "Non-repeatable",
                "Phantom"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "READ UNCOMMITTED",
                  "{red:allowed}",
                  "{red:allowed}",
                  "{red:allowed}"
                ],
                [
                  "READ COMMITTED",
                  "{green:prevented}",
                  "{red:allowed}",
                  "{red:allowed}"
                ],
                [
                  "REPEATABLE READ",
                  "{green:prevented}",
                  "{green:prevented}",
                  "{red:allowed}"
                ],
                [
                  "SERIALIZABLE",
                  "{green:prevented}",
                  "{green:prevented}",
                  "{green:prevented}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Defaults and Quirks",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:Postgres}, {blue:Oracle}: default ==READ COMMITTED==",
                "{orange:MySQL InnoDB}: default ==REPEATABLE READ==",
                "Postgres runs READ UNCOMMITTED as READ COMMITTED",
                "Postgres REPEATABLE READ = ==snapshot isolation==: blocks phantoms, allows **write skew**"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Postgres: set the level right after `BEGIN`. MySQL: `SET TRANSACTION` goes before `START TRANSACTION`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "BEGIN;",
                "SET TRANSACTION ISOLATION LEVEL SERIALIZABLE;"
              ],
              "note": "standard SQL form"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "text": "**Dirty vs phantom?** Uncommitted data vs newly committed rows. **Postgres REPEATABLE READ and phantoms?** Blocked, but write skew remains."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "SELECT FOR UPDATE and Row Locking",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "SELECT FOR UPDATE and Row Locking",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What it locks",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`SELECT ... FOR UPDATE` ==locks the returned rows== until COMMIT/ROLLBACK",
                "Other writers and other FOR UPDATE readers {red:block}",
                "Plain SELECTs {green:don't block} under MVCC"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Lock",
                "Other FOR SHARE",
                "Writers"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`FOR UPDATE`",
                  "block",
                  "block"
                ],
                [
                  "`FOR SHARE` (PG) / `LOCK IN SHARE MODE` (MySQL)",
                  "allowed",
                  "block"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Read-modify-write",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "BEGIN;",
                "SELECT bal FROM accounts",
                "  WHERE id = 1 FOR UPDATE;",
                "-- app computes new balance",
                "UPDATE accounts SET bal = 900",
                "  WHERE id = 1;",
                "COMMIT;"
              ],
              "note": "the row stays locked until COMMIT"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Prevents the ==lost update==: a second session waits, then reads the new value",
                "{blue:NOWAIT}: error immediately if a row is locked",
                "{green:SKIP LOCKED}: skip locked rows; the standard ==job queue== pattern"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Scope",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Postgres locks only the rows ==matched==",
                "Unindexed WHERE can lock {red:many rows}",
                "InnoDB locks ==every row it scans=="
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Lock by indexed key",
              "text": "Use `WHERE id = 1`, not a filter on an unindexed column."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Deadlocks and Common Mistakes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Deadlocks and Common Mistakes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a Deadlock Is",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "A holds lock 1",
                    "note": "wants lock 2",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "B holds lock 2",
                    "note": "wants lock 1",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Cycle: no progress",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "DB aborts a victim",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Victim gets an error: Postgres ==40P01==, MySQL ==1213==",
                "Victim must `ROLLBACK`, then be {green:retried}"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Prevention",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Lock in a ==consistent order==, e.g. lower account id first",
                "Keep transactions **short**",
                "Lock all needed rows up front, ordered by id"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "BEGIN;",
                "SELECT id FROM accounts",
                "  WHERE id IN (1, 2)",
                "  ORDER BY id FOR UPDATE;",
                "-- UPDATEs here",
                "COMMIT;"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common Mistakes",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Open transaction during user input or an API call: keeps locks, blocks ==vacuum==",
                "Do slow work {green:outside} the transaction",
                "No retry logic around deadlocks and `40001` failures"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Expect failure",
              "text": "Deadlocks (40P01, 1213) and SERIALIZABLE failures (==40001==) are normal. Retry the ==whole transaction==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Transactions Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Transactions Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Control",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`BEGIN;` ... `COMMIT;` persists, `ROLLBACK;` undoes everything",
                "`SAVEPOINT s;` marks a point inside the transaction",
                "`ROLLBACK TO s;` undoes work after s, transaction stays open",
                "`RELEASE SAVEPOINT s;` discards the marker"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Levels vs Anomalies",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Level",
                "Dirty",
                "Non-repeatable",
                "Phantom"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "READ UNCOMMITTED",
                  "{red:allowed}",
                  "{red:allowed}",
                  "{red:allowed}"
                ],
                [
                  "READ COMMITTED",
                  "{green:no}",
                  "{red:allowed}",
                  "{red:allowed}"
                ],
                [
                  "REPEATABLE READ",
                  "{green:no}",
                  "{green:no}",
                  "{red:allowed}"
                ],
                [
                  "SERIALIZABLE",
                  "{green:no}",
                  "{green:no}",
                  "{green:no}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Phantom under REPEATABLE READ is standard SQL only; ==Postgres== snapshots avoid it, InnoDB only for plain reads",
                "Set the level ==before the first statement=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "BEGIN ISOLATION LEVEL REPEATABLE READ;  -- Postgres",
                "SET TRANSACTION ISOLATION LEVEL SERIALIZABLE;"
              ],
              "note": "second form goes right after BEGIN"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Locks and Rules",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Clause",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`FOR UPDATE`",
                  "**exclusive** row lock"
                ],
                [
                  "`FOR SHARE`",
                  "**shared** row lock"
                ],
                [
                  "`NOWAIT`",
                  "fail fast if locked"
                ],
                [
                  "`SKIP LOCKED`",
                  "skip locked rows, job queues"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Keep transactions ==short==",
                "Lock rows in a ==fixed order==",
                "Default to READ COMMITTED; raise it only for a proven anomaly"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Retry",
              "text": "On `40P01`, `40001` or `1213`, ==ROLLBACK and retry== the whole transaction."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "In Postgres: BEGIN; INSERT succeeds; UPDATE fails on a unique violation; then you run SELECT 1. What happens?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "SELECT fails: ==current transaction is aborted==",
                "Only ROLLBACK, or ROLLBACK TO a savepoint taken before the UPDATE, recovers"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Under READ COMMITTED, T1 reads balance 100. T2 sets it to 50 and commits. T1 reads again. What does T1 see?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "==50==, a non-repeatable read",
                "At REPEATABLE READ in Postgres, T1 keeps seeing 100"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A updates row 1 then row 2. B updates row 2 then row 1, at the same time. What happens, and what is the fix?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Deadlock: one is aborted (Postgres 40P01) and must retry",
                "Fix: update rows in one fixed order, e.g. lowest id first"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
